## Execute Pipeline

The execute pipeline performs additional work for {{ dg.methodTerm }}. This pipeline is not limited to query execution methods, it may be called for any subscribed method — for example connection utility methods such as {{ dg.utilityMethodExamples }}.

Usages for this pipeline include:

- handling execution exceptions
- logging and measuring execution information
- caching execution results
- updating the host lists before executing the method
- catching network exceptions and performing the failover procedure
